From b3574a906dd59b04070d04b400ddc0efbed4c439 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artarex <22620496+Akrelion45@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 01:17:52 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Fix RenderingDevice thread ownership during shutdown

The separate render worker takes ownership of the main RenderingDevice,
but shutdown only resets the rendering server's thread ID. Device
destruction then calls finalize() from the main thread and fails the
device's thread guard.

Return the main device to the calling thread after the worker has stopped.
Keep the null check for backends without a RenderingDevice.

Validated with an empty project on Windows using Vulkan and D3D12,
comparing the official 4.8-dev5 build with a local patched build.
---
 servers/rendering/rendering_server_default.cpp | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/servers/rendering/rendering_server_default.cpp b/servers/rendering/rendering_server_default.cpp
index 82eebf5e8db7..213b0b6169f4 100644
--- a/servers/rendering/rendering_server_default.cpp
+++ b/servers/rendering/rendering_server_default.cpp
@@ -300,6 +300,13 @@ void RenderingServerDefault::finish() {
 	} else {
 		_finish();
 	}
+#ifdef RD_ENABLED
+	// The display server destroys the main device after the render worker
+	// has stopped. Return ownership to the calling (main) thread first.
+	if (RenderingDevice *rd = RenderingDevice::get_singleton()) {
+		rd->make_current();
+	}
+#endif
 }
 
